===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Grand Poobah}}

===Etymology===
From ''Pooh-Bah'', the name of a character in {{w|Gilbert and Sullivan|Gilbert and Sullivan's}} comic opera ''{{w|The Mikado}}'' (1885).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɹænd ˈpuːbɑː/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-grand poobah.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|colloquial|often|humorous}} A [[person]] who is [[important]] or [[high-ranking]].
#: {{ux|en|He once played golf with the '''grand poobah''' of their company.}}
# An extremely pompous person.

